    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 31</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">{LXXV} Gif mon wíf gebyccge, ⁊ sio gyft forð ne cume, agife þæt feoh ⁊ forgielde ⁊ gebete þam byrgean swa his borgbryce sie.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If a man makes a contract for a wife, but the marriage does not take place, let [the bride’s guardian] return the bride-gift and compensate [the groom], and pay the guarantor [the price] for the breaking of his surety.</ab>
        <ab type="secondTranslation" xml:lang="en">If anyone buys a wife and the marriage does not take place, he [the bride's guardian] shall return the bridal price and pay [the bridegroom] as much again, and he shall compensate the trustee of the marriage according to the amount he is entitled to for infraction of his surety.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Gif mon wíf byege, ⁊ seo gift forð ne cume, agife ðæt feoh ⁊ forgilde ⁊ gebete ðam byrgean, swa his borhbryce sy.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
